From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:52:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] agx: give each cube sample its own CEM scratch

The packer computed every cube sample's CEM in one shared scratch above
the register allocation. A cube array stages CEM's face in a seven-bit
PACK_SMPIR field, so for cube arrays that scratch had to sit below half
128, and the whole register file of any shader sampling a cube array was
capped at 112 halves. Counter-Strike 2's cube-array material shaders hold
far more than that live and spilled heavily.

Before RA, give each cube sample (but bias with minimum and scalar-
coordinate samples) a seventh source: an undefined four-word vector,
defined right before it, which emits no code. RA places it clear of every
value live at the sample, and below half 128 for a cube array
(texture_gpr); the packer computes that sample's CEM there. Cube arrays
lose the 112-half cap and plain cubes the eight halves reserved above the
allocation. Samples with their own scratch get a 176-half budget, which
keeps a heavy shader at 576 threads: Counter-Strike 2's cube-array
material passes ran faster at 177 halves than with the full 184 (185
halves, 512 threads), though they spill more there.

Counter-Strike 2's 1969 shaders (fossilize-replay of a capture): spills
9958 -> 3510, fills 13995 -> 4313, scratch -57%, instructions -1.9%; 181
shaders change, none with more instructions. The 90 cube-array shaders
go from ~240 to ~100 spills at 177 instead of 121 halves (832 -> 576
threads); 91 plain-cube shaders each free eight halves, several gaining
an occupancy step. In de_dust2 (two runs each, kernel job traces), the
median of the 50 longest render jobs fell from 1.60-1.65 ms to
1.00-1.22 ms; average fps is within run-to-run noise.

dEQP-VK cube and cube-array texture, shadow and GLSL texture-function
cases (2615, all cube arrays and a quarter of the rest): same results as
before, 586 pass, 0 fail. A cube-array pressure bench renders the same
image. test-agx3-cube-scratch checks the pass.

